        mc2:FileSpeciesEnum,
        mc2:ModelSpeciesEnum,
        mc2:SpeciesEnum ;
    skos:definition "Any one of several species of ruminants of the genus Ovis, native of the higher mountains of both hemispheres but most numerous in Asia; the domestic sheep, Ovis aries." .

NCIT:C14286 a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "Yeast" ;
    rdfs:subClassOf mc2:BiospecimenSpeciesEnum,
        mc2:DSPDatasetSpeciesEnum,
        mc2:DatasetSpeciesEnum,
        mc2:FileSpeciesEnum,
        mc2:ModelSpeciesEnum,
        mc2:SpeciesEnum ;
    skos:definition "Various single-celled members of the fungal families, ascomycetes, basidiomycetes and imperfect fungi that tend to be unicellular for the greater part of their life cycle." .

NCIT:C14287 a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "Zebrafish" ;
    rdfs:subClassOf mc2:BiospecimenSpeciesEnum,
        mc2:DSPDatasetSpeciesEnum,
        mc2:DatasetSpeciesEnum,
        mc2:FileSpeciesEnum,
        mc2:ModelSpeciesEnum,
        mc2:SpeciesEnum ;
    skos:definition "Brachydanio rerio, a species of small freshwater aquarium fish with a transparent embryo, making it possible to follow progeny of single cells until late stages of development; an important model for studies of vertebrate cell lineage and developmental biology." .

NCIT:C14303 a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "Worm" ;
    rdfs:subClassOf mc2:BiospecimenSpeciesEnum,
        mc2:DSPDatasetSpeciesEnum,
        mc2:DatasetSpeciesEnum,
        mc2:FileSpeciesEnum,
        mc2:ModelSpeciesEnum,
        mc2:SpeciesEnum ;
    skos:definition "A roundworm, most commonly Caenorhabditis elegans, that is used as a model organism in biological research." .

NCIT:C153598 a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "DNA Sequencing",
        "DNA-Seq" ;
    rdfs:subClassOf mc2:DSPDatasetAssayEnum,
        mc2:DatasetAssayEnum,
        mc2:FileAssayEnum,
        mc2:MeasurementTechniqueEnum,
        mc2:NGSLibraryStrategyEnum,
        mc2:PublicationAssayEnum ;
    skos:definition "The determination of the sequence of purine and pyrimidine bases in a strand of DNA.",
        "The determination of the sequence of purines and pyrimidines in deoxyribonucleic acid (DNA)." .

NCIT:C156056 a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "ATAC-Seq",
        "ATAC-seq" ;
    rdfs:subClassOf mc2:DSPDatasetAssayEnum,
        mc2:DatasetAssayEnum,
        mc2:FileAssayEnum,
        mc2:MeasurementTechniqueEnum,
        mc2:NGSLibraryStrategyEnum,
        mc2:PublicationAssayEnum ;
    skos:definition "A molecular genetic technique that isolates and sequences chromosomal regions that are rich in open chromatin. First, nuclei are harvested from a cellular sample. Then a hyperactive Tn5 transposase is added to the nuclei where it excises non-nucleosomal DNA strands and ligates co-administered high-throughput sequencing adapters (tagmentation).  The tagged DNA fragments are isolated, amplified by PCR and sequenced. The number of reads for specific region of DNA correlate with increased chromatin accessibility and this method can identify regions of transcription factor and nucleosome binding.",
        "Assay for Transposase-Accessible Chromatin (ATAC) strategy is used to study genome-wide chromatin accessibility. alternative method to DNase-seq that uses an engineered Tn5 transposase to cleave DNA and to integrate primer DNA sequences into the cleaved genomic DNA" .

NCIT:C156057 a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "MicroRNA Sequencing",
        "miRNA-Seq" ;
    rdfs:subClassOf mc2:DSPDatasetAssayEnum,
        mc2:DatasetAssayEnum,
        mc2:FileAssayEnum,
        mc2:MeasurementTechniqueEnum,
        mc2:NGSLibraryStrategyEnum,
        mc2:PublicationAssayEnum ;
    skos:definition "A next-generation or massively parallel high-throughput DNA sequencing-based procedure that can identify and quantify the microRNA sequences present in a biological sample.",
        "Random sequencing of small miRNAs" .

NCIT:C160998 a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "Rat" ;
    rdfs:subClassOf mc2:BiospecimenSpeciesEnum,
        mc2:DSPDatasetSpeciesEnum,
        mc2:DatasetSpeciesEnum,
        mc2:FileSpeciesEnum,
        mc2:ModelSpeciesEnum,
        mc2:SpeciesEnum ;
    skos:definition "Any of various rodent species of the genus Rattus, particularly Rattus norvegicus, that are widely used as model organisms in biomedical research." .

NCIT:C167284 a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "Reduced Representation",
        "Reduced Representation Bisulfite Sequencing" ;
    rdfs:subClassOf mc2:DSPDatasetAssayEnum,
        mc2:DatasetAssayEnum,
        mc2:FileAssayEnum,
        mc2:MeasurementTechniqueEnum,
        mc2:NGSLibrarySelectionMethodEnum,
        mc2:PublicationAssayEnum ;
    skos:definition "A DNA sequencing technique that can differentiate cytosine from 5-methylcytosine in a DNA sample. First, a denatured DNA sample is treated with bisulfite which converts non-methylated cytosine to uracil. Next, the sample is amplified using a PCR method that does not discriminate between non-methylated and methylated sequences. The amplified DNA is subjected to nucleotide sequencing. The resulting sequence is compared to an identical control sample of DNA that was not treated with bisulfite. Unmethylated cytosines will be displayed as cytosines in the control sample and as thymines in the bisulfite-treated sample.",
        "Reproducible genomic subsets, often generated by restriction fragment size selection, containing a manageable number of loci to facilitate re-sampling" .

NCIT:C16960 a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "Human Patient" ;
    rdfs:subClassOf mc2:BiospecimenSpeciesEnum,
        mc2:DSPDatasetSpeciesEnum,
        mc2:DatasetSpeciesEnum,
        mc2:FileSpeciesEnum,
        mc2:ModelSpeciesEnum,
        mc2:SpeciesEnum ;
    skos:definition "A human patient enrolled in a clinical study who receives medical attention, care, or treatment." .

NCIT:C172845 a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "ChIA-PET" ;
    rdfs:subClassOf mc2:DSPDatasetAssayEnum,
        mc2:DatasetAssayEnum,
        mc2:FileAssayEnum,
        mc2:MeasurementTechniqueEnum,
        mc2:NGSLibraryStrategyEnum,
        mc2:PublicationAssayEnum ;
    skos:definition "A molecular genetic technique that combines chromatin immunoprecipitation (ChIP) with paired end tagged (PET) DNA sequencing to identify the nucleotide sequences for the binding sites occupied by DNA-associated proteins in a sample.",
        "Direct sequencing of proximity-ligated chromatin immunoprecipitates." .

NCIT:C18136 a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "RT-PCR" ;
    rdfs:subClassOf mc2:DSPDatasetAssayEnum,
        mc2:DatasetAssayEnum,
        mc2:FileAssayEnum,
        mc2:MeasurementTechniqueEnum,
        mc2:NGSLibrarySelectionMethodEnum,
        mc2:PublicationAssayEnum ;
    skos:definition "Polymerase chain reaction that uses two sets of primers, in two sequential runs of amplification, with the second set intended to amplify a target within the first run product.",
        "Source material was selected by reverse transcription PCR" .

NCIT:C181927 a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "Multiplexed Immunohistochemistry",
        "mIHC" ;
    rdfs:subClassOf mc2:DSPDatasetAssayEnum,
        mc2:DatasetAssayEnum,
        mc2:FileAssayEnum,
        mc2:ImageAssayTypeEnum,
        mc2:MeasurementTechniqueEnum,
        mc2:PublicationAssayEnum ;
    skos:definition "A method that enables simultaneous detection of multiple biomarkers on a single tissue section using immunohistochemistry techniques.",
        "Multiplexed Immunohistochemistry (mIHC): a method that enables simultaneous detection of multiple biomarkers on a single tissue section using immunohistochemistry techniques." .

NCIT:C181928 a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "Multiplexed Immunofluorescence",
        "MxIF" ;
    rdfs:subClassOf mc2:DSPDatasetAssayEnum,
        mc2:DatasetAssayEnum,
        mc2:FileAssayEnum,
        mc2:ImageAssayTypeEnum,
        mc2:MeasurementTechniqueEnum,
        mc2:PublicationAssayEnum ;
    skos:definition "A method that enables simultaneous detection of multiple biomarkers on a single tissue section using immunofluorescence techniques.",
        "Multiplexed Immunofluorescence (MxIF): a method that enables simultaneous detection of multiple biomarkers on a single tissue section using immunofluorescence techniques." .

NCIT:C181930 a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "MIBI",
        "Multiplexed Ion Beam Imaging" ;
    rdfs:subClassOf mc2:DSPDatasetAssayEnum,
        mc2:DatasetAssayEnum,
        mc2:FileAssayEnum,
        mc2:ImageAssayTypeEnum,
        mc2:MeasurementTechniqueEnum,
        mc2:PublicationAssayEnum ;
    skos:definition "A method for multiplexed immunohistochemistry that uses secondary ion mass spectrometry to image antibodies tagged with isotopically pure elemental metal reporters. Multiplexed ion beam imaging (MIBI) is capable of analyzing up to 100 targets simultaneously over a five-log dynamic range. This technique enables comprehensive phenotypic profiling and spatial analysis of the tissue microenvironment.",
        "Multiplexed Ion Beam Imaging (MIBI): a method for multiplexed immunohistochemistry that uses secondary ion mass spectrometry to image antibodies tagged with isotopically pure elemental metal reporters, capable of analyzing up to 100 targets simultaneously over a five-log dynamic range." .

NCIT:C181931 a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "CODEX" ;
    rdfs:subClassOf mc2:DSPDatasetAssayEnum,
        mc2:DatasetAssayEnum,
        mc2:FileAssayEnum,
        mc2:ImageAssayTypeEnum,
        mc2:MeasurementTechniqueEnum,
        mc2:PublicationAssayEnum ;
    skos:definition "A highly multiplexed cytometric imaging approach that iteratively visualizes many protein targets in a single tissue staining reaction.",
        "CO-Detection by indEXing (CODEX): a highly multiplexed cytometric imaging approach used to create multiplexed datasets from a single tissue staining reaction. CODEX iteratively visualizes antibody binding events using DNA barcodes, fluorescent dNTP analogs, and an in situ polymerization-based indexing procedure." .

NCIT:C182027 a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "IMC",
        "Imaging Mass Cytometry" ;
    rdfs:subClassOf mc2:DSPDatasetAssayEnum,
        mc2:DatasetAssayEnum,
        mc2:FileAssayEnum,
        mc2:ImageAssayTypeEnum,
        mc2:MeasurementTechniqueEnum,
        mc2:PublicationAssayEnum ;
    skos:definition "A method that combines laser ablation of tissue specimens with mass spectrometry to image antibodies tagged with isotopically pure metals, enabling highly multiplexed spatial protein detection.",
        "Imaging Mass Cytometry (IMC): a method that combines laser ablation of tissue specimens with secondary ion mass spectrometry to image antibodies tagged with isotopically pure elemental metal reporters, allowing in situ characterization of the specimen while preserving its tissue architecture and cellular morphology." .

NCIT:C20218 a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "Human Cell Line" ;
    rdfs:subClassOf mc2:BiospecimenSpeciesEnum,
        mc2:DSPDatasetSpeciesEnum,
        mc2:DatasetSpeciesEnum,
        mc2:FileSpeciesEnum,
        mc2:ModelSpeciesEnum,
        mc2:SpeciesEnum ;
    skos:definition "A cell line established from human-derived cells that is maintained and propagated in vitro for research purposes." .

NCIT:C23011 a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "H&E",
        "Hematoxylin and Eosin Staining Method" ;
    rdfs:subClassOf mc2:DSPDatasetAssayEnum,
        mc2:DatasetAssayEnum,
        mc2:FileAssayEnum,
        mc2:ImageAssayTypeEnum,
        mc2:MeasurementTechniqueEnum,
        mc2:PublicationAssayEnum ;
    skos:definition "Hematoxylin and Eosin (H&E) staining: a routine histological staining method using two dyes, hematoxylin, which stains cell nuclei a dark purplish color, and eosin, which stains cytoplasm and connective tissue an orangish-pink color.",
        "Hematoxylin-and-eosin, or H&E, is a routine staining procedure of tissue sections. This staining method uses two separate dyes, one staining the nucleus and the other staining the cytoplasm and connective tissue. Hematoxylin is a dark purplish dye that stains the chromatin (nuclear material) within the nucleus. Eosin is an orangish-pink to red dye that stains the cytoplasmic material including connective tissue and collagen." .

NCIT:C2917 a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "Carcinoma In Situ",
        "Premalignant - in situ" ;
    rdfs:subClassOf mc2:BiospecimenCompositionEnum,
        mc2:DSPDatasetTumorTypeEnum,
        mc2:DatasetTumorTypeEnum,
        mc2:FileTumorTypeEnum,
        mc2:ManifestationEnum,
        mc2:PublicationTumorTypeEnum ;
    skos:definition "A malignant epithelial neoplasm which is confined to the epithelial layer without evidence of further tissue invasion.",
        "A neoplasm in which the malignant cells are confined to the epithelium of origin, without invasion of the basement membrane." .

EFO:0008722 a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "Drop-Seq",
        "Drop-seq" ;
    rdfs:subClassOf mc2:DSPDatasetAssayEnum,
        mc2:DatasetAssayEnum,
        mc2:FileAssayEnum,
        mc2:MeasurementTechniqueEnum,
        mc2:PublicationAssayEnum,
        mc2:VisiumSpatialLibraryConstructionMethodEnum ;
    skos:definition "A molecular genetic technique that combines chromatin immunoprecipitation (ChIP) with massively parallel DNA sequencing to map the binding sites of DNA-associated proteins in a sample of cells. First, crosslinked protein-DNA complexes are isolated using ChIP. Next, the crosslinks are broken, the proteins are removed and the purified DNA is modified with adaptor oligonucleotides to facilitate massively parallel DNA sequencing. Following sequencing, the DNA sequences that are obtained can be mapped to their genomic locations.",
        "Droplet microfluidics-based method for parallel analysis of mRNA transcripts from thousands of individual cells, in which each cell is co-encapsulated with a barcoded bead in a nanoliter droplet." .

